"Remote login is \ZbON\Zn.

On another Kilobyte: Internet > Remote Kilobyte
  computer:  ${addrs:-(no network address)}
  user:      $USER   (and its password)

From any other computer:  ssh $USER@${addrs%% *}" 14 66 || return
        kb_sudo && sudo systemctl disable --now ssh.service >/dev/null 2>&1
    else
        kb_dialog --title " Remote Login " --yes-label "Switch on" --no-label "Back" --defaultno --yesno \
"Remote login is OFF.

Switched on, everyone who knows a user name and its password can
use this computer over the network (SSH), for example with
Internet > Remote Kilobyte on another Kilobyte.
$(kb_is_live && printf '\n\\Z1On the live system the password of \"user\" is \"live\" and everybody\nknows it: change it first (Settings > Password).\\Zn')" 15 70 || return
